# how to copy artifact file from created application to s3 ?
what is artifact : it is snapshot of running application so that we dont want to rebuild it again and we can deploy it other server without rebuilding.
steps :
1) create s3 bucket and instance of c7i then and download jenkins ,maven,javaversion 17 and 21
2) install plugins s3 publisher,pipeline: aws steps and aws credintials then set credintials after that re-start jenkins
3) go to job create pipeline in script write down this : and change bucket name and give crediantials name as u given in jenkins credidentials 
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('pull') {
            steps {
               git branch: 'main', url: 'https://github.com/Rohit-1920/EasyCRUD-Updated.git'
            }
        }
        stage('build') {
            steps {
               sh '''cd backend
                mvn clean package -DskipTests'''
            }
        }
        stage('s3Upload') {
            steps {
               withCredentials([aws(accessKeyVariable: 'AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID', credentialsId: 'aws-cred', secretKeyVariable: 'AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY')]) {
                   // Fixed trailing comma, removed double .jar typo, and updated path to point inside backend directory
                   s3Upload acl: 'Private', bucket: 'jenkins-artifact-manager123', file: 'backend/target/student-registration-backend-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar', path: ''
               }
            }
        }
    }
}

4) finally build it.
